WEBVTT

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:17.000
I have rejoined the club.
Please take care of me.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:20.500
Okay! Give him some applause!

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:29.830
Right?! Right?!

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:33.290
Of course it'd turn out like this!
I knew this would happen!

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.080
Wait, what kind of expression is that?!
What is he feeling right now?!

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:41.200
Clap for me, at the very least!

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.950
Let's start practice.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:46.200
Please wait.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.620
"Third Year College Student
Taisei Uchinashi
Number 6, Left Flanker"
Are you really letting him back in?!

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:49.790
"Third Year College Student
Taisei Uchinashi
Number 6, Left Flanker"
Doesn't letting him back in mean

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:50.620
Doesn't letting him back in mean

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:53.450
that the club is fine with players
that skip practice and just suddenly quit?

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:56.830
Taisei. Ibuki has his reasons.

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:58.000
It's fine!

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.450
The team will get stronger
if Ibuki comes back!

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:04.830
Then, I'll be able to shine in more games!

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:08.830
He hasn't played for seven months.
He won't be of any use to us.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.700
That's for sure!

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:13.250
Stop it, guys!

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.620
I watched your matches.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:18.950
I'm pretty sure I'd be a lot of help.

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:20.040
Ibuki!

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.040
Bastard! What did you just say?!

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.500
Taisei, stop it!

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:27.620
Um, can I offer a suggestion?

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:32.700
Why don't we have Ibuki-<i>senpai </i>join
the B Team for our intraclub matches?

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:37.120
If he's completely useless,
we don't need him to join the team.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:41.290
Why do we have to go through the trouble
of doing something like that for him?

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:45.000
"A Team"       "B Team"
But, I think it would be a good idea...

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.660
"A Team"       "B Team"
Weren't you all planning on doing
a practice match tomorrow, anyway?

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.750
Well, I guess you're right!

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:52.450
I understand how you feel!

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:56.750
I mean, if you lost against a spineless
genius that hasn't played in a while,

00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:01.160
it would be the epitome of uncool.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:03.620
Oh, of course, he'd compensate you for it.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:07.000
If Ibuki-<i>senpai </i>is completely useless,

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:13.370
we'll have him work as a slave for
the rugby club until he graduates college.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:14.290
What?!

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:17.910
What? Really?! That'd be awesome!

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:20.080
Not only will he do the chores,

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:22.790
he'll respond to roll call for you
and collect class notes for you.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:24.540
He can save tables for you in the cafeteria

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:28.660
and use his stupidly excessive good looks
to set up match-making parties for you!

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:30.160
Seriously?!

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.370
I can get a girlfriend?!

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.540
Of course. He'll help until you get one.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:36.000
No, no, no, no! That's impossible!

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.790
He'd have to do something
about his face and personality!

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:41.830
Natsusa! I want to see seppuku!

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:43.500
Yes, an easy request.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:47.580
That's not easy at all.
You can't put a price on life.

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.910
What do you think, Captain?

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.870
Let's do it!

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:56.330
"B Team"
"Yunu" "Gotou" "Koreeda" "Nakase" "Sasano"
"Higashizaka" "Uematsu" "Satou" "Gou" "Kawaguchi"
"Tsudura" "U" "Sakamoto" "Morotomi" "Nakagawa"

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:01.000
"Ueoka"

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:39.500
I've done it now...

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.790
Why did I say such provoking things?

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:45.040
"I moved into a big house, but can't
get it all put away... Things keep piling up."

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:47.080
Your inner feelings of,
"I'm a genious! Seriously!"

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:49.080
accidentally came out.

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:53.200
You're wrong! I was just flustered because
the atmosphere was worse than I thought!

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.200
You guys completely ignored me, too.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:58.660
To begin with, didn't you say that you
already told them I was joining again?

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:00.160
I did.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:00.580
But it looks like 87 people read it
and ignored the message.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:04.000
"Read 87 People"
But it looks like 87 people read it
and ignored the message.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.540
My mental health!

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:09.910
Sei, don't just eat chicken tempura.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:12.910
Why did you suggest
something like that anyway?

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:16.870
I'll never be able to play
rugby again if I fail.

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:19.040
Don't get the wrong idea, okay?

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:23.250
I only like the Ibuki Ueoka
that is great at rugby.

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:26.580
If you're so weak that you fail here,
I have no more interest in you.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:30.000
Your feelings can change so easily!

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.540
Seiichirou!

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:34.330
Don't just sit there! Say something!

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:41.200
Considering the way you quit,
returning in a normal way would be impossible.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:43.950
Huh? You're super pissed...

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:45.410
Of course he is.

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:48.410
How many times did you
ignore Sei's messages?

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:52.660
When Sei is angry,
he's even quieter than usual.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:56.330
Yeah. You're the only one who'd
be able to tell the difference there.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:59.910
Anyway, please don't betray my expectations.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:14.500
Natsusa-<i>san</i>...

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:16.500
Do you think Ueoka-<i>san </i>is all right?

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.830
Huh? It'll be fine!

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:21.000
It'll be interesting whether
he wins or loses!

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.500
That's not okay at all!

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:30.040
To begin with... do you think the reserve
players and the B team would accept him?

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:33.160
Oh, you don't have to worry about that.

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:38.080
I-Ibuki-<i>senpai</i>!

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.160
D-Do you remember me?

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:43.250
I was in rugby school with you.

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:47.080
Oh! Yayoi! Long time no see! Doing well?

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.500
Y-Yes!

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:53.410
You've gotten taller. You were
this small in elementary school.

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:56.950
I-I wasn't that small!

00:06:56.950 --> 00:07:00.540
Oh! Kotori-<i>chan</i>, too! Long time no see!

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:03.250
Don't call ma first name!

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:04.700
Kotori!

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:07.700
Please don't call me that...

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:09.950
What kind of polite talk is that?

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:13.370
I said ta sto... Please stop...

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:14.370
Ibuki!

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:15.200
Senpai!

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:16.330
Ueoka!

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:18.830
Wow! He's really popular!

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:22.540
Right. He's been doing rugby
since he was in elementary school.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:25.700
He knows a lot of people
in the rugby world.

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:29.540
On top of that, he's a natural genius
with people, so he's popular.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:32.120
Especially among his juniors.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:34.660
He's really easy to talk to,
even though he was a star player.

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:36.700
So a lot of people admire him.

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:38.660
I think the reason a lot
of people didn't clap

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:42.250
was because they were being
polite to the third years.

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:45.330
I see. So that's how it is.

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:49.500
It's true that Ibuki-<i>senpai</i>
pissed everyone off when he quit.

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:53.700
The players in the same year hate him now,
but that's because they're mad

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:58.410
that he'd do something like that
without talking to them first.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:01.580
It's fine. He'll get the hang of things.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:05.120
Of course, as long as they
accept his rugby skills.

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:06.580
You're right!

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:11.040
You must of suggested this idea because
you believe in his skill, Natsusa-<i>san</i>.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:12.620
No. The chances are about 50-50.

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:14.790
Huh?! Really?!

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:16.370
That's right.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:22.370
The world of rugby isn't easy to come
back to after a seven-month blank.

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:28.870
But, please show me that your skills
can overcome that hurdle, Senpai.

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:30.120
"Fourth Year Student
Toranoshin Higashizaka
Number 19, Reserve"

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:32.870
"Fourth Year Student
Toranoshin Higashizaka
Number 19, Reserve"
Here we go! Don't drop it!

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:44.700
Ibuki! What the hell are you doing!
Stupid! Pass the ball!

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:46.540
Please wait.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:50.370
I'm so moved that I got a pass after so long...

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:52.330
That so? Well, guess it can't be helped...

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:54.580
Like hell! Stupid! Hurry up!

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:56.540
You have to get used to the ball!

00:08:56.540 --> 00:09:02.120
Tora-<i>nii</i>, you're so nice. This is the
first time you've ever been nice to me!

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:04.000
I love you. Hold me.

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:05.000
So gross!

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:06.700
What the hell is wrong with you?!

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:12.830
"Fourth Year Student
Makoto Someya
Number 10, Stand-Off"
Let me go!

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:14.040
--Why are you so strong?!

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:16.160
--Mako-<i>san</i>.
--Why are you so strong?!

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.750
Oh, Taisei.

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:18.830
Taku was looking for you just now--

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:24.290
The stand-off for this team is you,
Mako-<i>san</i>. Not him.

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:27.290
Too close!

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.450
Coming back after all this time...

00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:33.660
We need to show him that
there's no place for him here.

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:37.790
It's fine. I know.

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:54.830
"Doushisha University
Intraclub Match"

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:05.370
--Knock-on.
--It looks like he's not used to the ball yet...

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:07.950
Natsusa-<i>san</i>?

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:13.910
I can't wait... For Ibuki-<i>senpai</i>
to become a slave of the rugby club...

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:19.080
Huh? I felt a sudden chill...

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:22.040
"Team"           "First Half"         "Second Half"          "Total"

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:26.910
You're not exhausted at all, Senpai.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:28.330
Well, yeah.

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:32.120
Since I didn't have club activities
and I was skipping a lot of classes,

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:35.290
I used the time to run
and do weight training.

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:38.200
Probably even more than I did
when I was playing rugby?

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:40.040
It's true.

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:42.790
His body is a lot more built
than when he was playing rugby.

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:45.540
He had a lot more spring
to his movements, too...

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:47.620
I see.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:51.870
He did all the running and
weight training all alone...

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:54.910
More than when he played rugby...

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:56.750
So dark!

00:10:56.750 --> 00:11:00.200
I sincerely apologize for reconfirming again.

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:06.410
Yuzuki-<i>sama</i>, do you really wish for me
to return to the rugby club?

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:10.620
I do. So please try your best.

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:13.410
Your plays in the first half
were neither bad nor good.

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:18.830
You're doing pretty okay for
having a seven-month blank, but...

00:11:18.830 --> 00:11:22.120
I'm not interested in a
"pretty okay" version of you.

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:23.370
Scary! Scary! Scary! Scary!

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:24.330
Those eyes!

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:26.790
Don't push me further into a corner!

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:30.700
Please do better in the second half.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:41.370
You won't be able to return
as a player at this rate, you know?

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:42.910
I know.

00:11:42.910 --> 00:11:44.950
I've gotten a bit used
to the ball after the first half.

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:46.830
I'll take care of it in the second half.

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:48.950
You don't have to do anything.

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:53.700
I want to win the match, but it'd
be more fun to have you as a slave.

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:56.330
Hey, now...

00:11:56.330 --> 00:11:58.790
Why'd you suddenly come back?

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:03.660
I made a promise.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:06.450
What kinda promise?

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:08.660
Gross! Forget it!

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.290
Give me a sip!

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:14.700
So weak! It's so watered down! Gross!

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:16.330
Who made this?!

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:21.200
Ever since I was a kid, I've liked
my sport drinks watered down.

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:28.700
All right! Guess I'll give it
my all in the second half!

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:32.750
I told you that you don't need to try.
Stupid. Don't be so cocky.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.660
"Second Half"

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:44.700
It seems the regulars are
always stronger during scrum.

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:50.330
This guy!

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:53.950
Wow! That's the kind of tackle
you'd see overseas!

00:12:58.120 --> 00:13:00.080
Shit! I can't get through!

00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:04.450
Seriously, every time!

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:06.660
Why are you always in the perfect spot!

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:11.290
Run!

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:13.080
Huh? Who is he talking to?

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:18.040
Perfect timing!

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:24.160
Try.

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:29.750
Ibuki-<i>senpai</i>! You're a genius!

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:31.450
He's too amazing.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:34.540
How did he get to such a perfect
spot right after a tackle?

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:38.700
His turnover rate was too fast.
It's like he knew what was going to happen.

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:40.540
And, that kick of his...

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:45.620
Does that mean he knew where
Yayoi-<i>kun </i>was in this situation?

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:47.120
He's a genius...

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:49.290
The very definition of a genius!

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:15.200
Shit!

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:33.000
This brings back memories.

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:34.870
I'll lose if I get back-down.

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:49.450
What?!

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:52.830
Seriously! You piss me off!

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:56.450
Syouta!

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:57.790
He's here!

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:10.120
Tora-<i>nii</i>!

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:11.540
--What the hell!
--I love you! I love you! I love you!

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:12.870
--What the hell!
--I believed in you, Tora-<i>nii</i>!

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:16.080
--You're too happy about this!
--As expected!

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:16.660
--I knew you would pull through!

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:19.870
--Too close! Just get off of me!
--I knew you would pull through!

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:22.330
"Team"           "First Half"         "Second Half"          "Total"

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:26.200
Wow... They've turned the tables.

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:30.200
When I see him play, a certain
thought comes to mind.

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:37.290
I'm sure that he looks down
from the skies of the future.

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:40.500
He doesn't have a particularly large body.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:44.160
He doesn't have a part of him that
is physically exceptional compared to others.

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:50.000
He's just a genius when it comes
to reading plays on the field.

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:53.080
It doesn't matter if it's friend or foe.

00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:59.750
He moves as though he sees both
the <i>present </i>and the <i>future </i>of all 29 players.

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:04.750
I believe that isn't possible
unless you can see the skies of the future.

00:16:06.370 --> 00:16:09.830
But, that's how geniuses are.

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:15.250
He is a stand-off that is loved
by the god of rugby.

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:17.700
That's Ibuki Ueoka.

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:21.580
And a guy like that tried to quit...

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.040
I'm definitely going to bully him later.

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:26.700
Huh? Why?!

00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:31.410
He moves like that, even after a blank!

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:34.500
Makoto, calm down.

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:37.160
We're going to crush that cocky kid.

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:48.080
All right! If I continue getting
used to the ball like this...

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:04.250
Ouch!

00:17:06.410 --> 00:17:10.080
Trying to warm yourself up
on the field, Ueoka?

00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:12.870
That'll get you hurt.

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:15.000
Our biggest star has appeared.

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:19.370
So heavy?!

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:21.950
Was he this heavy?

00:17:34.660 --> 00:17:35.870
Try.

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:39.950
I'm surprised you had the guts to come back.

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:43.160
<i>Ex</i>-genius.

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:48.000
"Team"           "First Half"         "Second Half"          "Total"

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.290
"Team"           "First Half"         "Second Half"          "Total"
No side.

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:02.120
Wow!

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:05.910
That such surprisingly shitty game play!

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:09.700
Natsusa... We're here, too, you know.

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:13.250
B-But! Ibuki-<i>senpai </i>is really amazing!

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:14.870
We proved that point!

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:17.750
He should be able to join the club again, right?

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:25.620
W-Well, what do you think?

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:31.450
To begin with, the fourth years have
no qualms about him coming back.

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:34.450
That's right! The coach
already said it was okay, too.

00:18:34.450 --> 00:18:37.000
All that's left is the
third years talking it out.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:39.500
Tora! Let's get some chinese food!

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:42.290
We're celebrating Yuuki's new employment.

00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:44.790
Yuuki said he didn't want to celebrate.

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:46.580
Huh?! Why?!

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:49.330
"I can't believe they offered me a job!"

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:51.500
"There's no way this company is legit!"

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:52.830
Or something like that.

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:54.830
Isn't he too negative?

00:18:54.830 --> 00:18:59.910
Is he all right? He's the only one
who hadn't found employment yet...

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:03.000
Well, let's try to convince
him at the cafeteria.

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:04.450
The shorties should come, too.

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:06.410
Huh? Is that okay?

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:10.290
I-I'm not a shorty!

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:11.450
Whatever. Come on.

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:13.290
--Hey! Lemme go! Please!

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:16.290
--Are you going to put <i>natto</i>
on your curry again, Ikuto-<i>san</i>?
--Hey! Lemme go! Please!

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:18.080
Yeah. I think I'll have <i>natto </i>curry again.

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:20.370
That's just disgusting!

00:19:20.370 --> 00:19:22.660
You coming, Yuu?

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:23.700
Oh!

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:27.580
Go on, Yuu. It'll be fine.

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:28.790
Yes!

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:50.700
I can't take it anymore! I can't
handle this heavy atmosphere!

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:53.160
Please forgive Ibuki-<i>senpai</i>.

00:19:56.700 --> 00:20:03.080
Ibuki-<i>senpai </i>felt responsible for
my injuries, which was so unlike him.

00:20:03.080 --> 00:20:06.040
He stupidly quit the team and I was like,

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:11.410
"What is this guy doing?!
How pathetic! You're so stupid!"

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:16.040
So, I'm sure the people in the club
were even more troubled.

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:18.000
But, Senpai...!

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:23.040
I only have rugby.
Please let me play rugby here.

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:36.120
He's definitely an idiot who
doesn't think anything through...

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:40.370
I don't mind him coming back.

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:46.750
Playing with him reminded me how
good he is. He has good senses.

00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:49.950
That's right! Ibuki is good at rugby!

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:53.750
He makes me shine and he
said he'd show me hara-kiri?

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:55.450
No, like I said...

00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:58.040
And he'll set up match-making parties, right?

00:20:58.040 --> 00:20:59.700
No, that's not...

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:01.370
Hey, hold on! A guy like this--!

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:03.200
Of course we'll take him back.

00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:07.750
"Third Year College Student" "Li Hongbin"
"Number 14, Right Wing"
We should accept all players
who have the skills.

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:16.620
Th-Then!

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:21.410
--Ouch!
--Welcome back, Ibuki! Let's enjoy rugby!

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:25.250
Let's go eat meat to celebrate
your return. Your treat.

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:27.410
We should talk about the
match-making party, too.

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:29.370
Match-making and hara-kiri!

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:34.790
That'll cause an ambulance to come
and it'll become a serious incident!

00:21:34.790 --> 00:21:36.750
Should we go, too?

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:38.200
I'm not going.

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:39.700
Taisei!

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:45.870
Looks like things can't be solved that easily...

00:21:45.870 --> 00:21:50.580
Natsu, isn't today the day
you come back to the dorms?

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:52.950
I-I forgot!

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:55.580
We've already moved your stuff.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:57.450
Why panic about it?

00:21:57.450 --> 00:22:00.000
My heart isn't ready for it!

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.660
I mean, the person I'm going
to be rooming with...

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:43.330
"I can't win against a person
who enjoys everything so seriously."
Huh? There's only five seconds left
for the next episode announcement?!

00:23:43.330 --> 00:23:45.250
"I can't win against a person
who enjoys everything so seriously."
U-Um, to begin with,
if I do the announcement,

00:23:45.250 --> 00:23:46.950
"I can't win against a person
who enjoys everything so seriously."
Natsusa will say the the viewer ratings dro--
